<title>UK: Aluminium output up in Jan with new Asian data.</title>
<headline>Aluminium output up in Jan with new Asian data.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daily average primary aluminium output in January rose to 57,600 tonnes compared with 51,900 tonnes in December and 50,100 in January 1996, provisional figures from the International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) show.</p>
<p>Total production in January (31 days) was 1.785 million tonnes, compared with 1.608 million in December (31 days) and 1.552 million in January 1996.</p>
<p>The IPAI said Asian data for China, Tajikistan and Montenegro were included for the first time from January 1997.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of primary aluminium production was as follows (in thousands of tonnes) the IPAI said.</p>
<p>				Jan 97   Dec 96   Jan 96</p>
<p>    Africa		    93	 93	 70</p>
<p>    North America	  501	501	491</p>
<p>    Latin America	  179	179	178</p>
<p>    East/South Asia	318	148	141</p>
<p>    Europe West	    273	273	271</p>
<p>    Europe East/Central  278	269	267</p>
<p>    Oceania		  143	145	134</p>
</text>
